[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one issue, one fix queued. Its own table says otherwise.
The reports in it describe three problems, each with its own fix, so each has its own ticket now.

<Callout kind="warn">
Engineering update, 05 Oct: `parser` fixed (`fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`), `hint` won't fix (booking-v3 form retired).
Nothing has been done about `shift`: its ticket stays open.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} issues={{
  parser: 'https://github.com/BartekButrym/mega-s01e03-kb/issues/1',
  hint: 'https://github.com/BartekButrym/mega-s01e03-kb/issues/2',
  shift: 'https://github.com/BartekButrym/mega-s01e03-kb/issues/3',
}} />

## How the reports were split

- **One report, one id.** The export pages overlap, so some reports appear twice. Each id is counted once.
- **`parser` and `hint`** come from `causes.ts`, by tenant and channel, never from the intake tag. Intake guessed
  from the reporter's browser, and the guess disagrees with the tenant on dozens of reports.
- **`shift`** is the desk's own list of one-day moves (`desk-notes.json`). These reports describe a date one day off,
  or one meeting on two days in two cities. No swap of day and month explains that, so the parser fix cannot close them.
  As the desk counts, they stay in the `parser` row, where their tenant files them, and get their own ticket too.

## Why they were merged

Decision [0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject line alone. Every one of these reports says
some version of "wrong date", so subject matching put all three problems in one ticket.

